{"id":"5fcd1e5541654db5","group":"58","path":"58/batch17/58-thm-reversed-iteration.md","title":"Tail Factorization of a Reverse Easton Iteration","display":"thm-reversed-iteration — Tail Factorization of a Reverse Easton Iteration","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-reversed-iteration","aliases":["58-thm-reversed-iteration","Reverse Easton Iteration"],"display":"thm-reversed-iteration — Tail Factorization of a Reverse Easton Iteration","depends_on":["[[../batch15/58-df-zfc-two-step-iteration.md]]","[[../batch08/58-df-zfc-forcing10-forcing-equivalence.md]]","[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]","[[58-df-ordinal]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-reversed-iteration"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-reversed-iteration</span><span>Reverse Easton Iteration</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-reversed-iteration — Tail Factorization of a Reverse Easton Iteration"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"054f5df77a4bd18d\" href=\"?note=054f5df77a4bd18d\" title=\"../batch15/58-df-zfc-two-step-iteration.md\">../batch15/58-df-zfc-two-step-iteration.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"414860ba273020ea\" href=\"?note=414860ba273020ea\" title=\"../batch08/58-df-zfc-forcing10-forcing-equivalence.md\">../batch08/58-df-zfc-forcing10-forcing-equivalence.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-function.md\">../batch16/58-df-function.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"5582a281f15a33c2\" href=\"?note=5582a281f15a33c2\" title=\"58-df-ordinal\">58-df-ordinal</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\delta,\\beta,\\vec{\\mathbb P},\\vec{\\dot{\\mathbb Q}},\\vec{\\dot{\\mathbb R}}\\in V\">\\(\\delta,\\beta,\\vec{\\mathbb P},\\vec{\\dot{\\mathbb Q}},\\vec{\\dot{\\mathbb R}}\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Ord}\">\\(\\mathrm{Ord}\\)</span>（序数类，见 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"5582a281f15a33c2\" href=\"?note=5582a281f15a33c2\" title=\"58-df-ordinal\">58-df-ordinal</a>）</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb P_\\alpha\\coloneqq\\vec{\\mathbb P}(\\alpha)\">\\(\\mathbb P_\\alpha\\coloneqq\\vec{\\mathbb P}(\\alpha)\\)</span> 与 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\dot{\\mathbb Q}_\\alpha\\coloneqq\\vec{\\dot{\\mathbb Q}}(\\alpha)\">\\(\\dot{\\mathbb Q}_\\alpha\\coloneqq\\vec{\\dot{\\mathbb Q}}(\\alpha)\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ReverseEastonIteration}_S\\subseteq V^3\">\\(\\mathrm{ReverseEastonIteration}_S\\subseteq V^3\\)</span>（包含后继两步迭代及反 Easton 极限支撑条款的标准递归谓词）</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ReverseEastonTail}_S\\subseteq V^5\">\\(\\mathrm{ReverseEastonTail}_S\\subseteq V^5\\)</span>（给出阶段 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\beta\">\\(\\beta\\)</span> 至 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\delta\">\\(\\delta\\)</span> 的规范 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb P_\\beta\">\\(\\mathbb P_\\beta\\)</span>-尾迭代名）</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ReverseEastonTailFamily}_S\\subseteq V^4\">\\(\\mathrm{ReverseEastonTailFamily}_S\\subseteq V^4\\)</span>（此处定义的尾名族谓词）</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Function}\">\\(\\mathrm{Function}\\)</span> 与 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcForcing10ForcingEquivalence}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcForcing10ForcingEquivalence}_S\\)</span>（函数及强迫等价谓词）</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}reverse\\text{-}easton\\text{-}tail\\text{-}family}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{ReverseEastonTailFamily}_S\n(\\vec{\\dot{\\mathbb R}};\\vec{\\mathbb P},\\vec{\\dot{\\mathbb Q}},\\delta)\n\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{Function}\n(\\vec{\\dot{\\mathbb R}},\\delta+1,\\operatorname{ran}(\\vec{\\dot{\\mathbb R}}))\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\forall\\beta\\in\\delta+1\\;\n\\mathrm{ReverseEastonTail}_S\n(\\vec{\\dot{\\mathbb R}}(\\beta),\\vec{\\mathbb P},\\vec{\\dot{\\mathbb Q}},\\beta,\\delta).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}reverse\\text{-}easton\\text{-}tail\\text{-}family}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{ReverseEastonTailFamily}_S\n(\\vec{\\dot{\\mathbb R}};\\vec{\\mathbb P},\\vec{\\dot{\\mathbb Q}},\\delta)\n\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{Function}\n(\\vec{\\dot{\\mathbb R}},\\delta+1,\\operatorname{ran}(\\vec{\\dot{\\mathbb R}}))\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\forall\\beta\\in\\delta+1\\;\n\\mathrm{ReverseEastonTail}_S\n(\\vec{\\dot{\\mathbb R}}(\\beta),\\vec{\\mathbb P},\\vec{\\dot{\\mathbb Q}},\\beta,\\delta).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}reversed\\text{-}iteration}\\vdash{}&amp;\n\\delta\\in\\mathrm{Ord}\n\\land\\mathrm{ReverseEastonIteration}_S\n(\\vec{\\mathbb P},\\vec{\\dot{\\mathbb Q}},\\delta)\\\\\n\\to{}&amp;\n\\exists\\vec{\\dot{\\mathbb R}}\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{ReverseEastonTailFamily}_S\n(\\vec{\\dot{\\mathbb R}};\\vec{\\mathbb P},\\vec{\\dot{\\mathbb Q}},\\delta)\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land\\forall\\beta\\in\\delta+1\\;\n\\mathrm{ZfcForcing10ForcingEquivalence}_S\n\\bigl(\\vec{\\mathbb P}(\\delta),\n\\vec{\\mathbb P}(\\beta)*\\vec{\\dot{\\mathbb R}}(\\beta)\\bigr)\n\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}reversed\\text{-}iteration}\\vdash{}&amp;\n\\delta\\in\\mathrm{Ord}\n\\land\\mathrm{ReverseEastonIteration}_S\n(\\vec{\\mathbb P},\\vec{\\dot{\\mathbb Q}},\\delta)\\\\\n\\to{}&amp;\n\\exists\\vec{\\dot{\\mathbb R}}\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{ReverseEastonTailFamily}_S\n(\\vec{\\dot{\\mathbb R}};\\vec{\\mathbb P},\\vec{\\dot{\\mathbb Q}},\\delta)\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land\\forall\\beta\\in\\delta+1\\;\n\\mathrm{ZfcForcing10ForcingEquivalence}_S\n\\bigl(\\vec{\\mathbb P}(\\delta),\n\\vec{\\mathbb P}(\\beta)*\\vec{\\dot{\\mathbb R}}(\\beta)\\bigr)\n\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The iteration predicate is now an explicit antecedent; ordinal length alone cannot imply the factorization.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\beta\">\\(\\beta\\)</span> is bounded by the set ordinal <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\delta+1\">\\(\\delta+1\\)</span>, and the tail names form an explicitly guarded function.</li>\n<li>Reverse Easton support specifies the limit-stage support; it is not obtained merely by taking a limit over an arbitrary set of ordinals.</li>\n<li>The factorization reduces analysis of the full iteration to an initial segment and a tail forcing. Preservation of cardinals or large-cardinal properties still requires hypotheses on the iterands and supports.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch15/58-df-zfc-two-step-iteration.md","status":"resolved","id":"054f5df77a4bd18d","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch15/58-df-zfc-two-step-iteration.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch08/58-df-zfc-forcing10-forcing-equivalence.md","status":"resolved","id":"414860ba273020ea